Summary of modifications (GPL-3.0 §5a)
-------------------------------------

Starting from the QDuo source, Mtool has been modified as follows:

- Rebranded: product name, bundle identifier, configuration directory, Keychain
  service, menu-bar text, About page and documentation now refer to Mtool.
- Removed the upstream Aptabase analytics integration and the Sparkle
  auto-updater, and removed all references to the upstream author's release
  infrastructure, update feed, signing certificate and provisioning profile.
- Removed the restricted `keychain-access-groups` entitlement (which required the
  upstream author's Developer ID provisioning profile); API keys are now ordinary
  per-app Keychain items.
- Added a three-scenario router (`ContextRouter`, `ContextSnapshot`,
  `FocusedInputInspector`) driven by a configurable main shortcut.
- Added an optional double-tap Command trigger (`ModifierDoubleTapMonitor` /
  `ModifierDoubleTapDetector`).
- Added a local clipboard history with snippets (`ClipboardStore`,
  `ClipboardWatcher`, `ClipboardPanelController`) and its settings.
- Added a quick-search panel (`SearchPanelController`) and a screenshot-and-copy
  action.
- Replaced the default actions with research-oriented templates (translate,
  explain, read paper, polish, abstract).
- Rewrote the GitHub Actions workflow so it builds and packages an unsigned DMG
  without any upstream secrets.
